  model3DPath: "", model3DScale: 0, model3DRotation: [0, 0, 0], manualLightPositions: {}, riskRating: 4, 
  lightSettings: {}, hotspotSettings: {}, model3DHotspots: [], customLightNames: {}, author: "",
  drivingExperience: "The U06 223d xDrive is an exceptionally capable and potent daily driver. The 400Nm of torque provides a strong mid-range shove, making it an excellent highway cruiser that effortlessly climbs to higher speeds. Crucially, the 48V Mild Hybrid system completely eliminates traditional diesel turbo lag, providing instantaneous electric torque off the line. It runs noticeably smoother and quieter than older diesel generations. The xDrive AWD chassis is safe, grippy, and predictable in all weather conditions. Once the factory software restriction is removed via a Stage 1 tune, it completely transforms into a genuinely fast, punchy family vehicle while returning incredible fuel economy.",
  mechanicVerdict: "The B47 2.0L diesel is a massive, highly welcome step up in reliability from older engines. The B-series modular engines feature incredibly robust timing chains, curing the absolute worst nightmare of BMW ownership. The transverse mounting in the U06 chassis makes certain repairs tighter. The B47 is practically bulletproof, with one major exception: the EGR cooler. You MUST ensure the EGR cooler recall has been performed by BMW, as internal leaks can cause the intake manifold to melt and catch fire. The addition of the 48V ISG system adds electrical complexity, but mechanical reliability remains stellar.",
  repairCostEstimate: "$600 - $1,200 / year (Standard mechanical maintenance is highly predictable. Replacing a clogged intake manifold or worn engine mounts are the most common moderate bills. Crucially, you completely avoid the timing chain tax of older generations. If the EGR cooler is covered under recall, running costs are remarkably low, though 48V ISG or AdBlue system sensor replacements can occasionally be expensive)."
